<DOCUMENT source-infobase-name="Rules" content-collection-id="NYCrules" source-infobase-title="The Rules of the City of New York" base-output-dir="D:\process\NFOProcess\codes\ny\newyorkcity\NYCrules\output\CSRHNPHJPGBKCELW\" default-split-level="Chapter" makefile-filename="D:\process\NFOProcess\codes\ny\newyorkcity\NYCrules\output\CSRHNPHJPGBKCELW\NYCrules.mak" css-stylesheet-href="#!-- #ID=NYCrules_css_id --#" xml-output-dir="D:\process\NFOProcess\codes\ny\newyorkcity\NYCrules\output\CSRHNPHJPGBKCELW\XML\" css-stylesheet-name="NYCrules_css" makefile-document-depth="2">
	<LEVEL style-name="Chapter" style-name-escaped="Chapter" style-id="0-0-0-477" level-depth="2" toc-section="false">
		<RECORD id="0-0-0-155499" number="112930" version="3051">
			<HEADING>Chapter 20: Petitions for Agency Rulemaking</HEADING>
			<PARA>
				<DESTINATION id="0-0-0-20037" name="T66C020"/>Chapter 20: Petitions for Agency Rulemaking</PARA>
		</RECORD>
		<LEVEL style-name="Subchapter" style-name-escaped="Subchapter" style-id="0-0-0-480" level-depth="3" toc-section="false">
			<LEVEL style-name="Subtitle" style-name-escaped="Subtitle" style-id="0-0-0-15301" level-depth="4" toc-section="false">
				<LEVEL style-name="Part" style-name-escaped="Part" style-id="0-0-0-483" level-depth="5" toc-section="false">
					<LEVEL style-name="Subpart" style-name-escaped="Subpart" style-id="0-0-0-15960" level-depth="6" toc-section="false">
						<LEVEL style-name="Section" style-name-escaped="Section" style-id="0-0-0-486" level-depth="7" toc-section="true">
							<RECORD id="0-0-0-150950" number="112931" version="3051">
								<HEADING>§ 20-01 Definitions.</HEADING>
								<PARA>
									<DESTINATION id="0-0-0-20039" name="T66C020_20-01"/>§ 20-01 Definitions.</PARA>
							</RECORD>
							<LEVEL style-name="Normal Level" style-name-escaped="Normal-Level" style-id="0-0-0-0" level-depth="0" toc-section="false">
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155524" number="112932" version="3051">
									<PARA>As used in this chapter, the following terms have the following meanings: <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155523" number="112933" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<CHARFORMAT bold="1" italic="0" underline="0" strike-out="0" hidden="0">DSBS.</CHARFORMAT> “DSBS” means the New York City Department of Small Business Services or its successor in function. <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155522" number="112934" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<CHARFORMAT bold="1" italic="0" underline="0" strike-out="0" hidden="0">Person.</CHARFORMAT> “Person” means a natural person or a business entity, including but not limited to a corporation, trust, estate, partnership, cooperative, association, firm, club or society. <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155521" number="112935" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<CHARFORMAT bold="1" italic="0" underline="0" strike-out="0" hidden="0">Petition.</CHARFORMAT> “Petition” means a request or application for DSBS to adopt a Rule. <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155520" number="112936" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<CHARFORMAT bold="1" italic="0" underline="0" strike-out="0" hidden="0">Petitioner.</CHARFORMAT> “Petitioner” means the person who files a Petition. <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155519" number="112937" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<CHARFORMAT bold="1" italic="0" underline="0" strike-out="0" hidden="0">Rule.</CHARFORMAT> “Rule” has the meaning set forth in § 1041 of the City Administrative Procedure Act. <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155518" number="112938" version="3051">
									<PARA>(Added City Record 6/9/2026, eff. 7/9/2026) <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
							</LEVEL>
						</LEVEL>
						<LEVEL style-name="Section" style-name-escaped="Section" style-id="0-0-0-486" level-depth="7" toc-section="true">
							<RECORD id="0-0-0-155501" number="112939" version="3051">
								<HEADING>§ 20-02 Procedure for Submitting Petitions.</HEADING>
								<PARA>
									<DESTINATION id="0-0-0-20041" name="T66C020_20-02"/>§ 20-02 Procedure for Submitting Petitions.</PARA>
							</RECORD>
							<LEVEL style-name="Normal Level" style-name-escaped="Normal-Level" style-id="0-0-0-0" level-depth="0" toc-section="false">
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155516" number="112940" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>(a)<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<CHARFORMAT bold="0" italic="1" underline="0" strike-out="0" hidden="0">Content of petitions.</CHARFORMAT> Any person may petition DSBS to consider the adoption of a rule. The petition should be typewritten and must include the following information: <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155515" number="112941" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>(1)<TAB tab-count="1"/>A short statement of the purpose of the proposed rule, including an explanation of the problem or issue that the rule is intended to address and an explanation of how the proposed rule would serve to address the identified problem or issue; <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155514" number="112942" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>(2)<TAB tab-count="1"/>Proposed language for the rule; <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155513" number="112943" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>(3)<TAB tab-count="1"/>A short statement of any additional considerations that the Petitioner believes are relevant to DSBS’s determination on the petition; <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155512" number="112944" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>(4)<TAB tab-count="1"/>The name, address, telephone number, and email address of the Petitioner or the Petitioner’s authorized representative; <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155511" number="112945" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>(5)<TAB tab-count="1"/>The signature of the Petitioner or their representative. <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155510" number="112946" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>(b)<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<CHARFORMAT bold="0" italic="1" underline="0" strike-out="0" hidden="0">Submission of petitions.</CHARFORMAT> All petitions must be submitted to the Office of the General Counsel at the address/es identified on the DSBS website. <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155509" number="112947" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>(c)<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<CHARFORMAT bold="0" italic="1" underline="0" strike-out="0" hidden="0">Notice of change of contact information.</CHARFORMAT> The Petitioner must promptly notify DSBS of any change in their name, address, or telephone number during the period that the petition is under consideration by DSBS. <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155508" number="112948" version="3051">
									<PARA>(Added City Record 6/9/2026, eff. 7/9/2026) <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
							</LEVEL>
						</LEVEL>
						<LEVEL style-name="Section" style-name-escaped="Section" style-id="0-0-0-486" level-depth="7" toc-section="true">
							<RECORD id="0-0-0-155517" number="112949" version="3051">
								<HEADING>§ 20-03 DSBS Procedures for Considering and Responding to Petitions for Rulemaking.</HEADING>
								<PARA>
									<DESTINATION id="0-0-0-20043" name="T66C020_20-03"/>§ 20-03 DSBS Procedures for Considering and Responding to Petitions for Rulemaking.</PARA>
							</RECORD>
							<LEVEL style-name="Normal Level" style-name-escaped="Normal-Level" style-id="0-0-0-0" level-depth="0" toc-section="false">
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155507" number="112950" version="3068">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>(a)<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<CHARFORMAT bold="0" italic="1" underline="0" strike-out="0" hidden="0">Requests for supplemental information.</CHARFORMAT> DSBS will determine whether additional information is required that would assist DSBS in assessing the petition and may contact the Petitioner to request any additional information that it determines may be helpful to its determination. <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155506" number="112951" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>(b)<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<CHARFORMAT bold="0" italic="1" underline="0" strike-out="0" hidden="0">Timing of determinations.</CHARFORMAT> If a petition is submitted in proper form, as required by 66 RCNY § <LINK style-name="Jump" style-name-escaped="Jump" style-id="0-0-0-31" type="Jump" destination-name="T66C020_20-02" destination-id="0-0-0-20041">20-02</LINK>, within 60 days from the date of receipt of the petition, DSBS will either: <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155505" number="112952" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>(1)<TAB tab-count="1"/>deny the petition in writing, stating the reasons for denial; or <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155504" number="112953" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>(2)<TAB tab-count="1"/>approve the petition in writing, stating DSBS’s intention to initiate rulemaking, by a specified date, concerning the subject of the petition. <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155503" number="112954" version="3051">
									<PARA>
										<TAB tab-count="1"/>(c)<TAB tab-count="1"/>
										<CHARFORMAT bold="0" italic="1" underline="0" strike-out="0" hidden="0">Determinations.</CHARFORMAT> DSBS has full discretion to grant or deny any portion of a petition for proposed rulemaking and may amend or modify the petition’s proposed language. If a petition is denied in full, DSBS will take no further action. DSBS’s decision to deny or grant a petition is final and not subject to judicial review. <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
								<RECORD id="0-0-0-155500" number="112955" version="3051">
									<PARA>(Added City Record 6/9/2026, eff. 7/9/2026) <HIGHLIGHTER style="highlighter-ALP" original-style-name="ALP" style-name-escaped="highlighter-ALP" name="ALP" id="0-0-0-33">[ALP S-122]</HIGHLIGHTER>
									</PARA>
								</RECORD>
							</LEVEL>
						</LEVEL>
					</LEVEL>
				</LEVEL>
			</LEVEL>
		</LEVEL>
	</LEVEL>
</DOCUMENT>